kernel and its modules. A normal build starts with a configuration target and then
builds the default target:&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class="jose-wrapper"&gt;
 &lt;div class="jose-tools"&gt; &lt;span&gt;sh&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;button&gt;Copy&lt;/button&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;

 &lt;div class="jose-inner"&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;make defconfig
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;make -j&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;nproc&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The principal result is &lt;code&gt;vmlinux&lt;/code&gt;, an ELF executable. Architectures may additionally
produce bootable wrappers such as &lt;code&gt;bzImage&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;zImage&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;vmlinuz&lt;/code&gt;. Loadable modules
are ELF relocatable objects linked into &lt;code&gt;.ko&lt;/code&gt; files.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="source-and-output-trees"&gt;
 Source and Output Trees
 &lt;a href="#source-and-output-trees" class="heading-anchor"&gt;
 &lt;span&gt;#&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;An in-tree build has identical &lt;code&gt;srctree&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;objtree&lt;/code&gt;. An out-of-tree build keeps
generated files separate:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>